WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.280
Two hundred and fifty-two million years ago, before dinosaurs existed, saber-toothed predators and giant synapsids ruled a thriving prehistoric Earth.

2
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:20.140
Until the continental crust ripped open in Siberia, unleashing three million cubic kilometers of molten basalt in an eruption that burned for a million years.

3
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:32.500
Subterranean magma ignited massive ancient coal seams, pumping billions of tons of toxic sulfur into the skies and unleashing acid rain as caustic as battery acid.

4
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:42.200
As superheated seas choked and lost all oxygen, toxic bacteria turned the oceans purple, suffocating ninety-six percent of all marine species.

5
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:52.540
Continents turned into rotting wastelands. Every forest on Earth collapsed, triggering a planetary fungal spike feeding on millions of dead trees.

6
00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:04.390
Against impossible odds, a single burrowing survivor endured underground: Lystrosaurus, clearing the evolutionary stage for the rise of dinosaurs.

7
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.010
Life faced its closest brush with death. Without this catastrophic reset, we would never exist.
